      "body": "## Purpose\n\nReview feedback on #59422: vLLM should ask AITER for paged MQA logits and let AITER pick the kernel, instead of carrying a Gluon/FlyDSL switch that changes every time one of the kernels improves. This calls AITER's `paged_mqa_logits` (`from aiter.paged_mqa_logits import paged_mqa_logits`, imported lazily like `aiter.fused_moe`) for the sparse indexer decode logits on gfx942/gfx950. AITER picks Gluon or FlyDSL, and their launch knobs, from its tuned table (ROCm/aiter#6140), the same model as its fused-MoE dispatch.\n\nvLLM passes the same tensors it passes to the Gluon kernel today and no backend knobs (`ChunkK`, `WavePerEU`, `SplitKV`). When the installed AITER has no `aiter.paged_mqa_logits` module, the existing Gluon call runs unchanged, so this is a no-op until vLLM's AITER pin includes the op.\n\n## Dependency\n\nROCm/aiter#6140 (`aiter/paged_mqa_logits.py`, its tuned table and tuner).\n\n## Details\n\n- The 2D `(B, next_n)` `seq_lens` table is passed through as-is: `aiter.paged_mqa_logits` takes `[B]` or `[B, next_n]` and reduces to one length per sequence itself, so this path does not need #59420.\n- No change to the C4A / Triton / torch paths or to non-gfx942/gfx950 archs.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `pytest tests/v1/attention/test_rocm_aiter_paged_mqa_logits.py` (new): the AITER op gets the caller's tensors, the 2D `seq_lens` and only `Preshuffle` / `KVBlockSize`; the Gluon call runs when AITER lacks the op.\n- MI355X, real tensors through `rocm_fp8_paged_mqa_logits` with the 2D `seq_lens` table, against the torch reference, with ROCm/aiter#6140 installed. Shapes picked to hit both backends in the tuned table.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- Unit test: 2/2 pass on MI355X.\n- Real tensors (`AITER_LOG_TUNED_CONFIG=1` shows the pick):\n\n| batch | next_n | context | AITER pick | calc_diff vs torch |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 16 | 3 | 8192 | gluon ChunkK=128 WavePerEU=4 | 9.2e-11 |\n| 256 | 3 | 8192 | flydsl | 8.5e-11 |\n| 8 | 1 | 32768 | gluon ChunkK=256 WavePerEU=4 | 7.5e-11 |\n| 64 | 8 | 8192 | flydsl | 8.5e-11 |\n\n- Kernel level (from ROCm/aiter#6140, MI355X, GLM-5 indexer shape, batch 1..256, `next_n` 1..8): the tuned pick vs the Gluon `ChunkK=256, WavePerEU=2` this file passes today is -10.8% geomean at 8k context and -17.1% at 32k; FlyDSL is picked on 16 of 72 shapes, all at batch >= 32.\n- End-to-end serving benchmark and accuracy: not run yet.\n\n\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
